# Triage workspace state that is derived, bulky, or machine-specific.
#
# The evidence under data/ IS committed: a verdict nobody can re-check is just
# an assertion. What lives here instead is everything that can be regenerated.
#
#   .cache/compilers   ~1.2 GB of downloaded release binaries. Re-fetched on
#                      demand by `triage.py bisect`, and seeded for free from
#                      the DXC test tree with:
#                          triage.py catalog --seed-from build/tools/clang/test/dxc_releases
#   .cache/triage.db   the index. Rebuild it from the committed evidence with:
#                          triage.py reindex
#
# Note that `git clean -xdf` will delete the compiler cache. Nothing is lost
# but download time.
.cache/
